   "RaceName": "State Representative Pos. 2",
   "Statement": "<b>Elected Experience</b><br/><br/><p>State Representative (Assistant Ranking Member, Appropriations; Finance; Early Learning &amp; Human Services); Former Mayor (8 years), Councilmember (6 years), and Planning Commissioner (2 years), City of Orting; Former Chair, Pierce County Regional Council; Former Charter Review Commissioner, District 1.</p><br/><br/><b>Other Professional Experience</b><br/><br/><p>Executive Strategy, Penner &amp; Co; Veteran, United States Marine Corps: Iraq War Veteran &amp; Radio Operator.&nbsp;</p><br/><br/><b>Education</b><br/><br/><p>Harvard University, Master's (ALM); St. Martin's University, BA; Green River Community College, AA; Sumner High School.&nbsp;</p><br/><br/><b>Community Service</b><br/><br/><p>Co-Founder of PNW Vets, the largest Veteran support network in the Pacific Northwest; Crisis Intervention Trainer for WA-CJTC.</p><br/><br/><b>Statement</b><br/><br/><p>I grew up in Bonney Lake, graduated from Sumner High School, served as a Marine in Iraq, and led Orting as Mayor. As your Representative, I bring our community&rsquo;s shared values and that fighting spirit to Olympia.</p>\r\n<p>Together, we saved Buckley&rsquo;s Rainier School, prevented disastrous cuts for early education, protected care facilities for fentanyl-exposed newborns, and cut red tape to fund the repair of the White River and Fairfax bridges. &nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">With your support, I will keep fighting to lower living costs, demand accountability, protect our most vulnerable, and secure our neighborhoods. Let&rsquo;s lead with action, not talking points.</span></p><br/><br/>",
